{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the life of Sarah was.</b> Those who wish to calculate gematriot say: it is the numerical value of <b>ויהיו</b>. Her years of life were thirty-seven years, from the day Isaac was born until the day of the binding, when she died. But the ninety years she lived previously are not counted as life, for whoever has no children is considered as dead." "<b>A hundred years.</b> Rashi explained: therefore 'year' is written for each grouping, to say, etc. And if you ask: but in the case of Ishmael, 'year' is written for each grouping too? One may answer: where it writes 'a hundred,' it needs to write 'year' after it — there we do not derive the homily. But in the case of Sarah, it writes 'a hundred' and concludes without 'year,' and then writes 'year' after it — conclude from this that it comes for a homily. And what we derive in the case of Abraham, even though it writes in him 'a hundred' — that is because it writes in him 'ימי,' which is superfluous. Rashi also explained: a daughter of a hundred like a daughter of twenty for sin — just as a daughter of twenty did not sin. And if you ask: but is it not established that twenty-year-olds are subject to punishment? Rather, this is what it says: just as when she was twenty she was not subject to punishment — for at that period they were not subject to punishment until a hundred years; until twenty-four, for she was of the souls that they made in Haran, as is established as halakhah in the Tanna dei Eliyahu. So too when she was a hundred, by which time the giving of Torah had already passed and they were subject to punishment, she was without sin. Rashi also explained: a daughter of twenty like a daughter of seven for beauty — meaning she was beautiful without cosmetics and rouge and embellishment, as when she was twenty, for at that time it is the way of women to adorn themselves, as when she was seven, when there is no way to adorn. And in the Aggadah they interpret: a daughter of a hundred like a daughter of twenty for beauty, and a daughter of twenty like a daughter of seven for sin." "<b>The years of Sarah's life.</b> Rashi explained: all were equal for good. Even the seven, for we derive it only from seven and above. But in the case of 'the years of Ishmael's life' one cannot derive thus, for it has not yet specified his years; whereas here it writes <b>and the life of Sarah was</b> — if so, why do I need 'the years of Sarah's life'? Rather, conclude from this that it comes for a homily."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "The Hebrew reads 'ק׳ שנה' and 'מ״ת' — resolved as 100 years and 24 respectively based on the rabbinic source referenced (Tanna dei Eliyahu). Also 'כ׳‎' resolved as 20."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:29.184087699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}